From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: feuristic build <build@feuristic.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:26:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feuristic: exclusive USB modes, bulk-pipe class and
 usb_set_mode syscall
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New syshandles SYSHANDLE_USB_CCID and SYSHANDLE_USB_MSC.
- Kernel bulk-pipe class (firmware/kernel/usb) for CCID and MSC BOT,
  with a framed control channel (ZLP/STALL/events) so that all protocol
  parsing happens in the unprivileged coreapp.
- firmware/kernel/usb/usb_modes.c replaces the firmware branch of
  usb_config.c: NORMAL (FIDO HID + CCID [+ debuglink]), TIMESYNC (CDC-ACM)
  and IMPORT (MSC); feuristic VID/PID and strings; no WebUSB/WinUSB.
- SYSCALL_USB_SET_MODE / SYSCALL_USB_GET_MODE with verified parameters.
- Emulator: bulk-pipe interfaces carried as UDP datagrams; usb_start is
  idempotent and usb_stop no longer unregisters unused handles.
- trezorio: USBPipe (variable-length frames), usb_set_mode/usb_get_mode.

Feuristic-Rationale: spec §3 (USB architecture), §10.4 (hostile input
parsed unprivileged).

